# Fixed defect 2325, 2026-11-08, lane pm-use (found by panel 235's
# spec-warden): a dot where a `use` path's part belongs was told *a `use`
# path cannot climb*, whatever it was. `./` names the directory the path
# already stands in, and taking it out is certain, the line left reading the
# same file; a part that opens with a dot names a folder no `use` can spell,
# so a module there is no module of this program; `.` alone names a
# directory and no module, and `./` with no path after it is told so and
# repaired by nothing; only `..` climbs.
use fixedbugs2325/json/parse  #~ module_path_names_a_directory
use .heroes/json/parse  #~ module_path_dot_name
use fixedbugs2325/json/lines  #~ module_path_names_a_directory
use .  #~ module_path_names_a_directory
use ./  #~ module_path_names_a_directory
use ../json/parse  #~ module_path_climbs

function main()
    print(parse.x() + lines.y())
